ther, these complementary studies are expected to support a regulatory filing as early as 2029. Idorsia has aligned the development strategy of the Phase 3 program with the US FDA. The design of the program is also consistent with feedback received from the European Medicines Agency during previous regulatory interactions.\n\n### Milestones\n\n2026    FAB-KLEAR study initiated\n2026    New data and evaluation of long-term treatment                                                                         with lucerastat presented at WORLDSymposium™ 2026\n2021    Phase 3 open label extension study continued\n2021    Phase 3 study completed – primary endpoint not met\n2018     Phase 3 study initiated\n2016    Phase 1b study completed\n\n### Key scientific literature\n\n  * Nordbeck P., et al. Nature Communications, 10 January 2026 (online ahead of print).\n  * Wallace E., et al. Mol Genet Metab. 2026;147(2):109659.  \n  * Germain DP., et al. Mol Genet Metab. 2026;147(2):109423.\n  * Guérard N., et al. Clin Pharmacol Ther. 2018; 103(4):703-11.\n  * Welford RWD., et al. Hum Mol Genet 2018; 27(19): 3392-3403.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Lucerastat has been characterized over >6 years (https://www.idorsia.com/dam/jcr%3Aee110e37-d6dc-46c9-8617-c2b40d538ccb/Idorsia_company_presentation.pdf)\nciteturn183search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 weeks ago; Crawled: 4 days ago; # Lucerastat has been characterized over >6 years ... Investor presentation | October 2026\n# Lucerastat has been characterized over >6 years\n\n<visual_element id=\"e1\">\n\n**Clinical study timeline**\n\n**Study periods:**\n- Screening: 6–7 weeks\n- Treatment: 6 months\n- Open, uncontrolled, Extension (OLE): ongoing\n\n**Timeline milestones and treatment allocation:**\n\n| Milestone | Description | Patient count/status |\n|---|---|---|\n| Randomization | Randomization 2:1 | **118** patients randomized |\n| Primary/secondary efficacy endpoints | End 